{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configuring your user’s device ID with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class","doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/BrazeDelegate","doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/overrideResourceBundle"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Customize-Behavior","title":"Customize Behavior"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BrazeKit"},{"text":", a user can be identified using one of two device ID options:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/uidevice\/1620059-identifierforvendor","isActive":true},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A randomly generated UUID.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":" may not be available in all scenarios or devices, Braze provides the option to use a more generic UUID to identify a user’s device."}]},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The below configuration ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") is deprecated and will be removed in a future major release. After removal, the SDK will always use a randomly generated UUID as the device ID. Device IDs previously persisted from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":" continue to be respected until local persistence is cleared, at which point the device moves to a UUID-based device ID."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Setting-Your-Configuration","text":"Setting Your Configuration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To configure this option, set "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Braze.Configuration"},{"type":"text","text":". Assigning this property to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" will generate a random UUID for each user installation, whereas a value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" will notify the SDK to use the device’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"code":["let configuration = Braze.Configuration(","    apiKey: \"<BRAZE_API_KEY>\",","    endpoint: \"<BRAZE_ENDPOINT>\"",")","\/\/ Set this value to `true` to opt out of `identifierForVendor` usage.","configuration.useUUIDAsDeviceId = true","let braze = Braze(configuration: configuration)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Starting in 7.0.0, the default value for this property is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For device types that do not support "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":", such as watchOS or macOS, Braze will default to a randomly generated UUID regardless of which option is configured."}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After being generated, device IDs created from UUIDs will remain consistent throughout the lifetime of the application’s installation or until "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/wipeData()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called."}]},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/wipeData()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will erase all local SDK storage, the device ID that was previously stored will be deleted. Thus, if ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is enabled, the SDK will generate a new UUID for the device ID after this operation. Similarly, if ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is disabled, the SDK will re-use the same IDFV after this operation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Migrating-from-a-Previous-Version","text":"Migrating from a Previous Version"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are migrating your project from the legacy "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Appboy\/appboy-ios-sdk","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or from a version of the Braze Swift SDK prior to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5.7.0"},{"type":"text","text":", note that the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":" option will be used by default, regardless of the configuration setting. This ensures continuity for any anonymous users previously identified by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":" device ID."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In such cases, if you wish to override those pre-existing values and ensure that your "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId"},{"type":"text","text":" configuration is respected, call "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/wipeData()"},{"type":"text","text":" on the "},{"code":"Braze","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance after migrating to any version of the Braze Swift SDK from "},{"code":"5.7.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" onwards."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Device ID Configuration","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"BrazeKit"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/Braze\/device-id-configuration"},"references":{"https://github.com/Appboy/appboy-ios-sdk":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Appboy\/appboy-ios-sdk","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"AppboyKit SDK","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Appboy\/appboy-ios-sdk","title":"AppboyKit SDK"},"doc://Braze/documentation/BrazeKit/Braze/Configuration-swift.class/useUUIDAsDeviceId":{"title":"useUUIDAsDeviceId","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"useUUIDAsDeviceId"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Determines if a randomly generated UUID should be used as the device ID","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/brazekit\/braze\/configuration-swift.class\/useuui